<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raichur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raichur is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, with a fort begun in the late 13th century. It gives its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raichur-doab">Raichur Doab</a>, the fertile land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> and Tungabhadra rivers, which was fought over for centuries, first by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> and later by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> and the Bahmani and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a> sultanates. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a> of Vijayanagara won a major victory at Raichur in 1520.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raichur.jpg" alt="Raichur" width="320" height="137" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tanzeelahad · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Aam_Talab,_Raichur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
